/T (Chosen system: Q2 k-NN with 20 irrelevant features \(22 total\). The two useful measurements are overwhelmed by independent distractors after standardisation. Q2 validation accuracy falls from 91.0% with no distractors to 74.5% with 20; the average nearest/farthest distance ratio rises from 0.0214 to 0.4308. This is primarily feature-representation and distance-concentration failure rather than insufficient training or an intrinsically poor k value. )
/E (Chosen system: Q2 k-NN with 20 irrelevant features \(22 total\). The two useful measurements are overwhelmed by independent distractors after standardisation. Q2 validation accuracy falls from 91.0% with no distractors to 74.5% with 20; the average nearest/farthest distance ratio rises from 0.0214 to 0.4308. This is primarily feature-representation and distance-concentration failure rather than insufficient training or an intrinsically poor k value. )
/Pg 24 0 R
