/Count -1
/Next 1144 0 R
>>
endobj
1042 0 obj
<<
/Title (E. Implement and validate with matched splits \(2 marks\))
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 810 0 R
/Prev 1145 0 R
/First 1146 0 R
/Last 1146 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 938 0 R
>>
endobj
1043 0 obj
<<
/Title (Yes: mean validation accuracy increases from 73.8% to 93.8%, a 20.0-percentage-point gain, exceeding the predeclared +5-point target. All three training-only screenings selected original feature columns 0 and 1. Average measured prediction time per 1,000 queries changes from 5.57 ms to 5.41 ms. Active vector size falls from 22 numbers to 2 \(about a 90.9% reduction\).)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 938 0 R
/Next 1044 0 R
>>
endobj
1044 0 obj
<<
/Title (The gain is substantial on this generator and matched evaluation, but is not proof the same mutual- information filter will succeed with interacting features or distribution drift. The original all-feature model remains preferable if every recorded attribute is demonstrably predictive, feature scoring is unreliable, or high-dimensional metric learning is already available. A future check should repeat on independent datasets and reserve a separate untouched test for assessing the final redesigned strategy.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 938 0 R
/Prev 1043 0 R
>>
endobj
1045 0 obj
<<
/Title (Extract the project ZIP. Install dependencies from requirements.txt, change directory to Programs, and execute python run_all.py. The relative folders Datasets, Results, Graphs, Diagrams and Outputs contain the input records and outputs. The seven Python programs are also individually executable. Output text captured from actual individual runs is included in Outputs/*_execution.txt. No unavailable software or specialised hardware was required.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 940 0 R
>>
endobj
