/Title (At k=1, Voronoi cells define a jagged class boundary sensitive to small changes and noisy labels: low bias but high variance. Increasing k pools more points and typically smooths the boundary; k approaching the full training size moves toward majority-class prediction, high bias and lower variance. With eight samples, a tie is possible at k=8, so the stated tie rule matters. Confirmation requires repeated stratified validation, learning curves, and changes in training-versus-validation error on larger labelled samples, not only the single illustration.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1199 0 R
/First 1226 0 R
/Last 1226 0 R
/Count -1
